sections.Overview:
A difficult & exposed scramble connecting the base of Victoria Ravine to the top of Victoria Gully by taking a diagonal scramble line & exposed ledge traverse across the South-West face of Separation Buttress. This route uses sections of WT Cobern & CW Campbell's 1916 route and Martin Versfeldts Variation to this, briefly outlined in the 1936 MCSA Journal. The route has one very short (~3m) but exposed C/D scramble and several more exposed C scrambles & ledges, a rope & trad gear is strongly recommended due to the exposure.
Be aware that this is a very remote part of the mountain, escape routes are few and far between. The terrain is undisturbed and therefore loose and overgrown in some sections;
Do not attempt unless very experienced.

